---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import aasha from '../data/aasha.json';
import AashaQuestions from '../components/AashaQuestions.astro';
const headExtra = `<title>Aasha Child Development &amp; Early Intervention Centre | Greater Noida</title><meta name="description" content="Individualised child development care at Aasha, Greater Noida: psychiatric consultation, developmental assessments, speech therapy, occupational therapy, special education and behavioural support."><link rel="canonical" href="https://mindgracencr.in/aasha"><meta property="og:title" content="Aasha Child Development &amp; Early Intervention Centre"><meta property="og:description" content="Where hope meets development. Explore our team, therapies and family-centred care pathway."><meta property="og:image" content="https://mindgracencr.in/assets/images/Aasha_early_intervention_logo.webp"><meta property="og:url" content="https://mindgracencr.in/aasha"><meta property="og:type" content="website"><link rel="stylesheet" href="/assets/css/min/seo-pages.min.css">`;
const steps = [
 ['Connect and consult', 'Begin with Dr. Anita Sharma to discuss your concerns, your child’s development and everyday experiences. You do not need a diagnosis first—describe what you notice at home and school.'],
 ['Assess and understand', 'Dr. Sana Firdos plans clinical and psychometric assessments around your child’s strengths, challenges and diagnostic needs. Screening tools can indicate that a closer look is warranted; they never decide a child’s future alone.'],
 ['Plan together', 'The team develops an individualised roadmap with the appropriate combination of occupational therapy, speech therapy, behavioural support or special education. Goals are agreed with you and tied to real situations, not to making a child appear typical.'],
 ['Intervene and review', 'Therapy begins in a nurturing environment. Progress is reviewed and the plan adjusted as your child’s needs change. If a strategy increases distress rather than participation, it is reconsidered.'],
 ['Empower and integrate', 'With your involvement and consent, we work with families and schools to help skills carry into home, learning and community life.']
];
---
<Layout headExtra={headExtra}>
<main id="main-content" class="seo-page">
<section class="seo-hero">
<img class="aasha-logo" src="/assets/images/Aasha_early_intervention_logo.webp" alt="Aasha Early Intervention Centre" width="240" height="160" fetchpriority="high">
<p class="seo-kicker">Aasha: Child Development &amp; Early Intervention Centre · Greater Noida</p>
<h1>Empowering every child to reach their full potential.</h1>
<p class="seo-answer">Aasha Child Development &amp; Early Intervention Centre in Gamma 2, Greater Noida provides individualised developmental assessments, speech therapy, occupational therapy, special education, behavioural support and child psychiatric consultation. Care is led by Dr. Anita Sharma and Dr. Sana Firdos. All child-related care on this website comes under Aasha.</p>
<div class="seo-actions"><a class="btn" href="#contact">Book an Assessment</a><a class="btn btn-outline" href="#services">Explore Our Services</a></div>
</section>
<section class="seo-section" id="about"><h2>Welcome to Aasha: where hope meets development</h2><p>Every child holds a unique universe of potential. At Aasha in Greater Noida, we nurture, guide and support children facing developmental, behavioural and learning challenges.</p><p>Our multidisciplinary team brings psychiatry, clinical psychology and therapy together to create individualised plans around each child’s neurological, emotional and everyday needs. We combine clinical care with empathy to help children build skills for school, home and community participation.</p></section>
<section class="seo-section" id="leadership"><h2>Guided by expertise, driven by compassion</h2><div class="seo-grid"><article class="seo-card"><h3>Dr. Anita Sharma</h3><p><strong>Consultant Psychiatrist &amp; Clinical Director</strong></p><p>Dr. Sharma oversees clinical care and long-term intervention planning, aligning medical, psychological and therapeutic goals. Her approach helps children and parents feel heard and supported from the first consultation.</p><a href="/dr-anita-sharma">Meet Dr. Anita Sharma</a></article><article class="seo-card"><h3>Dr. Sana Firdos</h3><p><strong>Clinical Psychologist &amp; Head of Assessments</strong></p><p>Dr. Firdos leads cognitive, behavioural and developmental evaluations using standardised psychometric and developmental tools. Findings help families understand their child’s needs and guide an individualised intervention plan.</p></article></div></section>
<section class="seo-section" id="approach"><h2>The Aasha approach</h2><div class="seo-grid"><article class="seo-card"><h3>Individualised therapy</h3><p>Assessment findings and clinical oversight shape a plan for your child’s specific strengths, needs and goals. Two children with the same diagnosis can need very different support.</p></article><article class="seo-card"><h3>Parents as partners</h3><p>Clear communication and parental coaching help you support your child’s progress beyond the clinic. You know your child best; your observations guide the plan.</p></article><article class="seo-card"><h3>Meaningful milestones</h3><p>We agree practical goals with families and review communication, independence, regulation and participation over time—asking for a break, starting a task, tolerating a change of plan. Progress varies for each child.</p></article><article class="seo-card"><h3>A nurturing environment</h3><p>A warm, sensory-friendly setting helps children feel comfortable, engaged and ready to learn. Harmless movement or a quiet child is not automatically a problem to correct.</p></article><article class="seo-card"><h3>Honest about evidence</h3><p>We explain what assessments and therapies can and cannot do. Diets, supplement stacks and expensive test packages marketed as autism cures are not part of our care plans; concerns about them belong in the open, at the appointment.</p></article></div></section>
<section class="seo-section" id="services"><h2>Integrated care under one roof</h2><div class="seo-grid">{aasha.services.map(service => <article class="seo-card"><h3><a href={`/aasha/${service.slug}`}>{service.name}</a></h3><p>{service.answer}</p></article>)}</div></section>
<section class="seo-section" id="conditions"><h2>Conditions and concerns we support</h2><ul><li><strong>Neurodevelopment:</strong> autism spectrum disorder (ASD) and attention deficit hyperactivity disorder (ADHD)—which can co-occur, and whose overlapping behaviours need careful evaluation rather than guesswork.</li><li><strong>Motor and sensory needs:</strong> cerebral palsy, sensory processing difficulties, and gross and fine motor delays.</li><li><strong>Cognition and learning:</strong> intellectual disabilities, global developmental delay, dyslexia, dysgraphia and dyscalculia.</li><li><strong>Communication and behaviour:</strong> speech and language delays, aggression, self-injurious behaviour, tantrums and emotional dysregulation.</li><li><strong>School concerns:</strong> academic difficulties, attention and school refusal.</li></ul><p>Some signs deserve a quicker conversation: no pointing or babbling in infancy, no single words around 16 months, no two-word phrases around two years, or any loss of skills a child used before. You do not need to match every item on a checklist—persistent concern is reason enough. Assessment helps identify which support is appropriate. Explore <a href="/adhd-autism-assessment">ADHD and autism assessments</a>, <a href="/learning-disability-assessment">learning assessments</a> and <a href="/child-student-mental-health">child and student mental health</a>.</p></section>
<section class="seo-section" id="journey"><h2>Your roadmap to development</h2><ol>{steps.map(([name, description]) => <li><h3>{name}</h3><p>{description}</p></li>)}</ol></section>
<section class="seo-section"><h2>A message from our clinical director</h2><blockquote><p>“At Aasha, we understand that receiving a developmental diagnosis for your child can feel overwhelming. Our mission is to replace that anxiety with action, clarity, and hope.”</p><p>— Dr. Anita Sharma, Consultant Psychiatrist</p></blockquote><p>We are committed to walking alongside families, bringing medical expertise and individualised therapies together so children and parents feel supported.</p></section>
<section class="seo-section" id="referrals"><h2>For medical professionals and referring partners</h2><p>Aasha welcomes collaboration with paediatricians, neurologists and schools across Greater Noida and the NCR region. Contact our coordination team about referrals, professional progress reports and a clinical detailing session.</p><p>Our multidisciplinary approach complements medical management with developmental, behavioural and therapeutic support. Information sharing with referring professionals and schools is coordinated with family consent.</p><a class="btn btn-outline" href="tel:+919667863295">Discuss a referral</a></section>
<AashaQuestions />
<section class="seo-section"><h2>A moment to reflect on your child’s development</h2><p>Our single-child check-in helps you organise everyday observations for a conversation with a professional. It is a discussion aid, not a diagnostic test.</p><a class="btn" href="/aasha/developmental-check-in">Start a developmental check-in</a></section>
<section class="seo-section" id="contact"><h2>Visit Aasha / book an assessment</h2><address>Aasha Child Development &amp; Early Intervention Centre<br>J-123, J Block, Gamma 2, Greater Noida, Uttar Pradesh 201310.</address><p><strong>Monday to Saturday:</strong> 12:00 PM–8:00 PM<br><strong>Sunday:</strong> Closed</p><div class="seo-actions"><a class="btn" href="tel:+919667863295">Call +91 96678 63295</a><a class="btn btn-outline" href="/book">Request an assessment</a><a href="/location">Directions and location</a></div></section>
<section class="seo-section"><h2><a href="/aasha/learning">Autism and ADHD learning library</a></h2><p>Explore eight sourced guides and three printable worksheets for assessment, everyday support, nutrition and understanding treatment claims.</p><p><a href="/aasha/learning#guides">Read the guides</a> · <a href="/aasha/learning#resources">Print family resources</a></p></section>
</main>
</Layout>
<style>.aasha-logo{display:block;width:240px;max-width:100%;height:160px;object-fit:contain;background:white;border-radius:16px;margin-bottom:1.5rem} .seo-section li{margin-bottom:1rem} address{font-style:normal}</style>
